# Bitmovin

> Bitmovin provides modular video infrastructure — cloud encoding for live and on-demand video, cross-platform player SDKs, playback analytics and AI scene analysis — used by broadcasters, streaming services and sports leagues to run video workflows at scale.

Bitmovin's products are modular: Player, VOD Encoding, Live Encoding, Observability, AI Scene Analysis, Streams and Stream Lab. They can be adopted individually or combined into an end-to-end workflow.

Bitmovin is not a CDN, CMS, MAM, or subscriber-management system.

Website: https://bitmovin.com
Expanded version of this file: https://bitmovin.com/llms-full.txt

## Products

- [Player](https://bitmovin.com/llms/player.md): Cross-platform adaptive-streaming player for Web, iOS, Android, tvOS, Roku, smart TVs and games consoles. Supports HLS, DASH and progressive delivery, with DRM, client- and server-side ad insertion (CSAI/SSAI) and analytics built in.
- [VOD Encoder](https://bitmovin.com/llms/vod-encoder.md): Cloud encoding for on-demand video with per-title optimization, multi-codec output (H.264, H.265/HEVC, AV1, VP9), HDR conversion and DRM packaging, running across AWS, GCP, Azure and OCI.
- [Live Encoder](https://bitmovin.com/llms/live-encoder.md): Low-latency live encoding with RTMP, SRT, Zixi and HLS ingest, SCTE-35 ad signalling, live-to-VOD workflows, standby pools for instant channel start, and SSAI integrations including YoSpace, AWS MediaTailor and Broadpeak.
- [Observability](https://bitmovin.com/llms/observability.md): Real-time playback analytics across QoS and QoE metrics — startup time, rebuffering, error rates, bitrate, CDN performance and engagement — with per-session drill-down and cross-dimensional analysis.
- [AI Scene Analysis](https://bitmovin.com/llms/ai-scene-analysis.md): Scene-level metadata extracted during encoding: scene boundaries, summaries, visual elements, mood, IAB taxonomy classification, sensitive-content flags and automatic ad-placement markers, with multi-language output.
- [Streams](https://bitmovin.com/llms/streams.md): Managed end-to-end video delivery for simpler use cases — upload, encode and embed via a web component.
- [Stream Lab](https://bitmovin.com/stream-lab/): Automated playback testing across 30+ physical devices, including Samsung, LG and Vizio TVs, browsers and games consoles.

